    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Researchers from Pakistan, China, the US and the UK have collaborated to produce a 3D map of all 46 chromosomes in a human nucleus at the prophase stage - the earliest phase when a cell starts preparing for division - in a move that could generate new insights into how the human genome is organised during development and disease.",
